      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/canyon_city_oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Canyon City serves as the county seat of Grant County and was platted in 1862.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/canyon_city_oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Up to ten thousand miners once flocked to Whiskey Gulch during the early stages of the gold rush.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canyon_City%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Canyon City honors the renowned poet Joaquin Miller, who was known as the Poet of the Sierras.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
